window.docContents[3].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Composition.StatementModel/#file-Computational___Specifications___Composition___StatementModel":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Composition › StatementModel.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 121 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nMulti-session model composition with costed reductions (Lemma 3, L3)Trusted: the statement. Read with Computational/Specifications/Game/ModelIface.lean (modelIface and KeyIndAdvantageForHandshake), Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/KeyInd1KeyReal.lean (pqxdhKeyIndImpl1KeyReal), and Computational/Specifications/Reductions/Pqxdh/StatementPqReds.lean (CompositionCostedReductions, CompositionCostedReductionFamily, and CompositionCostedReductionFamilyBounded). See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.ModelSecure S ℓ states Lemma 3 (label L3, proved as model_secure_costed in Computational/Theorems/Lemmas.lean) for the one-key real-HKDF handshake ki := SignalPqxdh.pqxdhKeyIndImpl1KeyReal S P. It asserts a budget-indexed family of ReductionDsl reductions reds : CompositionCostedReductionFamily S ℓ P C K qep decT encT (kindRed against ki and two-stage prefixRed k against single-session SM.gameR) whose syntactic step-cost, query, and block-size bounds CompositionCostedReductionFamilyBounded hold unconditionally in P.Under SignalPqxdh.WellFormedPrimitivesδ P (which supplies the byte-length laws for fixed-width ReductionDsl handshake simulation) and ModelAdversaryPerInstanceBounded A b qStart qs, instantiating R_e2e := reds b qStart qDR qInst yields a KeyInd adversary advK within keyIndReductionBudget S qStart b, stage-2 adversaries making at most qs k queries, and ComposedAdvantage (modelIface … ki …) A ≤ 2 · KeyIndAdvantageForHandshake S P ki advK + ∑ k < qStart, ⨆ flip, …, where each summand is the single-session SM.gameR bias of (R_e2e.prefixRed k).eval2 mixed over stage 1. Because composition stops at single-session SM.gameR, no single-session primitive or message-counter assumptions appear here.\n\n\n\ndef composedIsInstQueryL58–62 ↗#Whether a composedSpec query targets secure-messaging instance k.\n\ndef ModelAdversaryPerInstanceBoundedL64–81 ↗#Query bounds for an adversary A of G(Σ_model): bounds random-oracle, initiator, responder, total KeyInd, non-RO KeyInd, startDR (≤ S.N_send_tot and ≤ qStart), per-instance ratchet (≤ qs k for k < qStart), and total ratchet (≤ ∑ k < qStart, qs k) queries.\n\ndef ModelSecureL83–119 ↗#Multi-session model composition (Lemma 3, L3) with costed reductions over ki := SignalPqxdh.pqxdhKeyIndImpl1KeyReal S P: bounds ComposedAdvantage in G(Σ_model^ki) by twice the KeyInd advantage against ki plus the sum over promoted sessions k < qStart of the worst-flip single-session SM.gameR bias mixed over stage 1 of prefixRed k.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Composition/StatementModel.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Composition.StatementModel/#file-Computational___Specifications___Composition___StatementModel"},"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.LibsignalCli.StatementPqElf/#file-Computational___Specifications___LibsignalCli___StatementPqElf":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli › StatementPqElf.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 303 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (12)def realPow8def realScalarMuldef realScalarAdddef realUnreachedPrimsBasedef realXeddsaSigndef realIsValidDhTripledef realUnreachedPrimsdef CliPqxdhExcusedAbortabbrev withExcusedAbortTermdef CliPqxdhSecurityForabbrev CliPqxdhElfSecuredef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecure\n\n\n\nELF-direct security statement for the PQXDH CLITrusted: the statement. Defines CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecure, the top-level correctness and cryptographic security predicate instantiated at cliElfBytes in Computational/Theorems/Main.lean. Read alongside StatementPq.lean (cliPqExp, CliPqxdhAdvantage), StatementPqOomGame.lean (CliPqxdhFlagProb, CliKemFailProb), StatementPqReds.lean, Computational/Specifications/Assumptions/Kyber1024Correct.lean (KyberNoiseGap), LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/KEM/Kyber1024KeyGen.lean (kyber1024KemKeyGen), LibsignalBinary/Specifications/CryptoGames/DH/X25519Group.lean (X25519Pt, x25519Dh, x25519EncPt, x25519EncT, x25519DecT, x25519Delta), and LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/CliBinaryPq.lean (CliPqxdhElfCorrect, cliRunElf, resolveCliElfAddrs). See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md and Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md.CliPqxdhSecurityFor S ℓ ForRuns is stated at the closed primitive bundle realPEParams (FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 / SHA-512 compression, FIPS 197 AES-256, RFC 7748 X25519, round-3 Kyber-1024 encapsulation/decapsulation, FIPS 203 ML-KEM-768 incremental), the concrete Curve25519 prime-order x-only subgroup (X25519Pt, x25519Dh, x25519EncPt, x25519EncT, x25519DecT, explicit point-fiber bound x25519Delta = 1 / 2 ^ 250), and the concrete Curve25519/XEdDSA and round-3 CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 unreached model operations (realUnreachedPrims CryptoGames.MLKEM.kyber1024KemKeyGen: x25519Base, scalar arithmetic mod edOrderL, cofactor-clearing subgroup projection realPow8, real XEdDSA signing realXeddsaSign, reference DDH predicate realIsValidDhTriple, and concrete Kyber-1024 key generation kyber1024KemKeyGen). It asserts cost- and query-bounded reductions (L_cli, RK, D, reds) and establishes two upper bounds in ℝ≥0∞ on CliPqxdhAdvantage for the runs selected by ForRuns: first against KeyInd1KeyRealAdvantage, and second (given the HKDF random-oracle idealization gap KeyIndRoGap, DEV-CLI16) against pqxdhKeyIndAdvantageBoundActiveδ (GapSigEufCma, KemShCr, GapDhWithSign). Both bounds instantiate the Kyber-1024 decapsulation failure parameter to ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112 under the SHA3-512 (G) + SHAKE-256 (PRF) CBD-noise idealization gap KyberNoiseGap ε (DEV-PQ21; key-generation wire lengths (1568, 3168) are discharged unconditionally by kyber1024_kem_delta_correct), and include the Double Ratchet prefix sum prefixSum, 2 * CliKemFailProb evaluated directly on the adversary A (since adversary-chosen send randomness controls the SPQR V1 ML-KEM-768 coins), and, when exc? = some exc, 2 * CliPqxdhFlagProb for excused aborts (withExcusedAbortTerm). The only remaining primitive premise on kyber1024KemKeyGen is the ≤ 1 / 2 ^ 255 public-key collision bound _hKemColl (which cannot be proved unconditionally for concrete unkeyed SHA3-512 G without an idealization on SHA3-512; see DEV-PQ21). The KEM-generic counterpart over an arbitrary kemKeyGen and δ_kem lives in StatementPqElfAnyKem.lean (CliPqxdhSecurityForAnyKem).CliPqxdhElfSecure specializes CliPqxdhSecurityFor to the ELF-direct runner cliRunElf elf addrs using the 23 .symtab-resolved addresses addrs (resolveCliElfAddrs: 18 Rust panic entry points and 5 SampleNTT entry points), starting directly from plain ElfImage.loadState (zero initial memory patches), with exc? := some (CliReachesSampleNttStuckElf elf addrs) (adding the 2 * CliPqxdhFlagProb SampleNTT seed-divergence term via withExcusedAbortTerm, DEV-CLI22) and no .OutOfMemory hypothesis or allocation-failure term on the security clause (under the modelled 1 GiB dynamic physical-memory budget; the correctness conjunct CliPqxdhElfCorrect excuses both .OutOfMemory, DEV-CLI15, and SampleNTT seed divergence, DEV-CLI22). Every instruction except the 18 Rust panic entry points (DEV-E7) executes directly from plain loaded ELF memory, including aes and spqr CPU-feature probes against the pinned auxv (AT_HWCAP = 0x1b, AT_HWCAP2 = 0: FP, ASIMD, AES, and PMULL enabled, ATOMICS/LSE = 0; AT_RANDOM = 16 zero bytes); the trust point is that the ELF .symtab labels the 18 panic entry points and 5 SampleNTT entries accurately.Scope follows Computational/docs/DEVIATIONS.md: unpartnered first-message payload privacy and authentication are covered by the Auth conjunct of Lemma 1 rather than folded into this game (DEV-C5), and as in CliBinaryPq.lean, the statement applies to the modelled auxv (AT_HWCAP = 0x1b, LSE bit 8 = 0, DEV-CLI10) and excludes subsequent calls after an accepted non-matching pre-key recv (DEV-CLI11).\n\n\n\nConcrete Curve25519 / XEdDSA unreached PQXDH primitives\n\n\n\ndef realPow8L98–112 ↗#Cofactor-clearing idempotent subgroup projection on Curve25519 (gexp_div_8): raises points on E(𝔽_p) to 3 * edOrderL + 1 (≡ 0 mod 8, ≡ 1 mod edOrderL) and points on the quadratic twist E'(𝔽_p) to 3 * twistOrderL + 1 (≡ 0 mod 4, ≡ 1 mod twistOrderL), mapping non-32-byte inputs to 0^32.\n\ndef realScalarMulL114–119 ↗#32-byte little-endian Curve25519 scalar multiplication modulo edOrderL.\n\ndef realScalarAddL121–126 ↗#32-byte little-endian Curve25519 scalar addition modulo edOrderL.\n\ndef realUnreachedPrimsBaseL128–139 ↗#Base UnreachedPqxdhPrimitives bundle fixing sigPkGen, scalarMul, scalarAdd, and pow8 to Curve25519, with placeholders for sigSign and isValidDhTriple populated in realUnreachedPrims.\n\ndef realXeddsaSignL141–159 ↗#Concrete XEdDSA signing over realPEParams (SHA-512, Ed25519 scalar multiplication and point compression, Curve25519 scalar arithmetic mod edOrderL), packing the Edwards sign bit of [a]B into bit 7 of byte 63.\n\ndef realIsValidDhTripleL161–165 ↗#Concrete Curve25519 DDH-oracle predicate matching SignalPqxdh.isValidDhTripleRef over realPEParams and realPow8.\n\ndef realUnreachedPrimsL167–174 ↗#Concrete UnreachedPqxdhPrimitives at realPEParams: fixes all 6 Curve25519/XEdDSA fields (sigPkGen, sigSign, scalarMul, scalarAdd, pow8, isValidDhTriple), leaving only Kyber-1024 kemKeyGen parameterized.\n\nCanonical CLI PQXDH security proposition\n\ndef CliPqxdhExcusedAbortL178–181 ↗#Holds when i is a PQXDH-mode input (CliPqxdhInputs W) excused by exc on which run i has no outcome or aborts (run i = none ∨ run i = some .aborted).\n\nabbrev withExcusedAbortTermL183–191 ↗#Adds 2 * CliPqxdhFlagProb … (CliPqxdhExcusedAbort exc run W) to rhs when exc? = some exc, or leaves rhs unchanged when exc? = none.\n\ndef CliPqxdhSecurityForL193–267 ↗#Canonical CLI PQXDH security statement at realPEParams, the concrete Curve25519 prime-order x-only subgroup (X25519Pt, x25519Dh, x25519EncPt, x25519EncT, x25519DecT, x25519Delta = 1 / 2 ^ 250), and round-3 CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 key generation CryptoGames.MLKEM.kyber1024KemKeyGen with concrete decapsulation failure parameter ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112 under SignalPqxdh.KyberNoiseGap ε (DEV-PQ21; key-generation wire lengths (1568, 3168) proved unconditionally by kyber1024_kem_delta_correct, public-key collision bound _hKemColl retained as a premise), parameterized by the run quantifier ForRuns over (run, exc?). Asserts cost- and query-bounded reductions and bounds CliPqxdhAdvantage against KeyInd1KeyRealAdvantage and (given KeyIndRoGap) pqxdhKeyIndAdvantageBoundActiveδ. Cost bounds (CliAdapterCostBounded, CompositionCostedReductionFamilyBounded) track both total queries qTot = b.q_total + qStart + qDR and per-kind counts (bhKindCounts b qStart qDR) separating online queries (b.q_on, qStart, qDR) from offline random-oracle queries (b.q_ro), while the KeyInd bound depends only on b_ki.q_on.\n\n\n\nELF-direct security statements\n\nabbrev CliPqxdhElfSecureL282–292 ↗#Specializes CliPqxdhSecurityFor to the ELF-direct runner cliRunElf elf addrs at the closed primitive bundle realPEParams, the concrete Curve25519 prime-order x-only subgroup (X25519Pt, x25519Dh, x25519Delta = 1 / 2 ^ 250), and round-3 CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 key generation kyber1024KemKeyGen (δ_kem = ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112 under KyberNoiseGap ε), with exc? := some (CliReachesSampleNttStuckElf elf addrs) (for the 2 * CliPqxdhFlagProb SampleNTT seed-divergence term, DEV-CLI22) and no .OutOfMemory hypothesis.\n\ndef CliPqxdhBinaryCorrectAndSecureL294–301 ↗#bytes parses as elf, the 23 .symtab addresses resolve via resolveCliElfAddrs, and both CliPqxdhElfCorrect elf addrs and CliPqxdhElfSecure S ℓ elf addrs hold.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli/StatementPqElf.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.LibsignalCli.StatementPqElf/#file-Computational___Specifications___LibsignalCli___StatementPqElf"}});